	"equipment": [
		{
			"id": "e9i7eomzCXJRwwNlG",
			"description": "Autogun",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The standard-issue solid-slug battle rifle of regiments and militias that lack a lasgun allocation — a recoil-operated intermediate-calibre rifle that recurs across Astra Militarum background material as the \"poor cousin\" of the lasgun, more common on low-priority garrison and PDF postings.\n\nDesign: Fixed autogun anchor, 7d pi, holding lasgun parity (per framework.md: \"Lasgun parity against flesh... stopped by carapace\"). Average roll 24.5 gets through flak (DR 30) on 9.4% of hits and mesh (DR 36) on 0.3%, notably worse than the lasgun's own 97.8%/90.6% because the autogun has no armour divisor and a solid slug has no focusing trick to help it through DR the way a lasgun's beam does; against carapace (DR 70) it penetrates 0% of hits, confirming \"stopped by carapace\" even more emphatically than before. This is an honest consequence of a family with no divisor, not a departure from the lasgun-parity design goal, which is measured against flesh (HP), not DR. Range 500/2000 fits an intermediate-calibre rifle. RoF 10, 30(3) follow selective-fire rifle conventions. The Dum-Dum usage applies the same expanding-round logic as the autopistol's Manstopper. Handling: min ST corrected to 9 (√(10×8)≈8.9), matching the same formula correction applied to the 8 lb lasgun patterns in this project's las.yaml. Bulk -4 and Rcl 2 are unchanged.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"tech_level": "7",
			"legality_class": "3",
			"base_value": "150",
			"base_weight": "8 lb",
